---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Farm advice for every phone">
  <h1>AgriVoice</h1>
  <p>Weekly farm brief, weather alerts, market prices and answers to common questions for smallholder farmers in Nigeria. It works on any phone through a USSD menu (no data needed) and on this light website.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/demo/">Try the phone simulator</a> <a class="btn secondary" href="/brief/">Open the farm brief</a></p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Farmers with basic phones:</strong> dial the USSD code, no internet needed.</li>
    <li><strong>Farmers and extension agents with smartphones:</strong> the same information here, with voice notes.</li>
    <li><strong>Village price agents:</strong> <a href="/prices/report/">send market prices</a> with your agent code.</li>
    <li><strong>Admins:</strong> <a href="/admin/">manage content</a> and approve prices.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A <a href="/brief/">weekly farm brief</a> for your state and crop, written and approved by people.</li>
    <li>Weather for the next days and alerts for heavy rain, dry spells and heat.</li>
    <li>Recent <a href="/prices/">market prices</a> from village agents, approved before they show.</li>
    <li><a href="/ask/">Answers to common questions</a>, or a call-back request when nothing fits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How to dial</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p>A live Nigerian short code comes after funding. For now, use the <a href="/demo/">simulator</a>, or the Africa's Talking sandbox with the code shown in your sandbox channel settings.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">Some content is placeholder and labelled <span class="badge">Demo data</span>. No advice here is generated by AI. Weather data by Open-Meteo.com.</p>
</Base>
